{{!-- The fold caret on its own, for sections with no edit pencil to sit beside.
      Rendered INSIDE the heading (which becomes its positioning context), unlike
      the pencil-bearing sections where section-edit-toggle emits it into the
      section's top-right corner — either way the sheet finds the heading from the
      caret and folds the run of content below it. Caller passes `collapse`, the id
      the fold is remembered under.

      `defaultCollapsed` starts the section SHUT for a user who has never touched it,
      for sections that are reference rather than content (the GM Toolkit's prep
      reference). The stored preference records sections sitting against their
      default, so an id saved for one of these means the user pushed it open; see
      utils/section-editing.js.

      The aria-expanded and title below are the un-wired defaults. Both are restated
      by `_wireSectionCollapse` at wire time, before paint, from the section's actual
      state, so a default-collapsed caret does not announce itself as expanded. --}}
<a class="stonetop-section-collapse" data-section="{{collapse}}"{{#if defaultCollapsed}} data-default-collapsed="true"{{/if}} role="button" tabindex="0"
   aria-expanded="true" title="Collapse section"><i class="fas fa-caret-down"></i></a>
